<title>FRANCE: Danone denies bidding for Italy's Parlamat.</title>
<headline>Danone denies bidding for Italy's Parlamat.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>French food group Danone denied a market rumour on Wednesday that it was interested in bidding for Italian food firm Parmalat Finanziaria.</p>
<p>&quot;Danone denies this rumour,&quot; a spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>Danone, which rose earlier after brokerage UBS said the stock was undervalued and upgraded its recommendation to buy, was 4.04 percent higher at 746 francs at 1345 GMT. The bourse's CAC-40 index was up 1.1 percent.</p>
<p>Brokers said the acquisition rumour was fanned by a two percent rise in Parmalat shares on the Milan bourse.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
